{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164704-the-demon-blooded-dhampir","id":1164704,"title":"The Demon-Blooded Dhampir","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-02T17:34:37-08:00","id":1164704,"title":"The Demon-Blooded Dhampir","content":"I have a thing for combining splats that should probably stay separate, so on reading Half-Damned, several interesting new concepts occurred to me - such as wolf-blooded or demon-blooded Dhampir.<br /> <br /> I'm still not entirely sure what kind of stories might be interesting to explore with such characters, though. Perhaps a character that's the 'end result' of a long line of Ordo-Dracul research, some sort of Proto-Deviant?<br /> <br /> Does anyone else plan to explore Dhampir like this? How do you plan to do it? Any mechanical pitfalls to watch out for? Any unique stories you could see such a combination working well for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T21:47:50-08:00","id":1164735,"title":"","content":"As an aside, this is absolutely an Ordo experiment somewhere.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, It appears to be simple at this point. Tells, special merits, etc all stack. So do the weaknesses. I would say there is a limit (no wolfblooded dhampiric fractals) and it makes less sense in some cases (proximi dhampir strike me as some wrong, as do fae-touched dhampir) but that os a table by table basis.<br /> <br /> As for stories...I will get back to you on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T23:20:51-08:00","id":1164740,"title":"","content":"Considering you can have vampire and changeling wolf-blooded I wouldn't consider a dhampir or ghoul or revenant as something you couldn't give a Tell to.<br /> <br /> Most people's aversion to template stacking seems to be an overly dramatic reaction to a NPC from World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> More realistically, a problem you'll have is that a demon-blooded or dhampir game is meant to be at a certain power level, and when one player has twice the 'power' of the others it's possible they're playing a character who is objectively more advantageous. It also can act to change the focus of the story a bit, as they are all generally tied to larger settings, dhampir to Vampire, fractals to Demon and so forth. If these are not problems, for whatever reason, then go wild. Have dhampir mages. If you're willing to put more work into the homebrew and ignore people on the forum telling you that it's impossible, have vampire mages, or demon vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-03-2017, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T00:19:15-08:00","id":1164742,"title":"","content":"What was that Broken Covenant that dealt with angels again? The Tenth Choir, was it? From what I hear of it, dhampir are created with a purpose of the vampire\u2019s part, right? Maybe a vampire of the Tenth Choir had to do something with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T04:15:32-08:00","id":1164753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164704-the-demon-blooded-dhampir?p=1164740#post1164740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most people's aversion to template stacking seems to be an overly dramatic reaction to a NPC from World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>And even then, template (ok it wasn't really templates back then, but you know what I mean) stacking being bad was the wrong lesson to draw. The right lesson was pet NPC's are bad, but the OWoD remained <i>rife</i> with those.<br /> <br /> But anyway, back on topic. A wolf-blooded dhampir sounds fine to me. Fitting even, since in dhampirs' folklore of origin, werewolves and vampires weren't particularly distinct.<br /> <br /> Demon-blooded, why not? The God-Machine as presented in Demon seems somewhat &quot;orthogonal&quot; to the rest of the supernatural, so I don't see its heritage reacting with vampirism in a way that would make them incompatible.<br /> <br /> Connections to the supernal are fragile outside of full mages, so I agree with FallenEco about Proximi-dhampirs being an unlikely mix (though I don't see a problem with fae-blooded ones).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More realistically, a problem you'll have is that a demon-blooded or dhampir game is meant to be at a certain power level, and when one player has twice the 'power' of the others it's possible they're playing a character who is objectively more advantageous. </div> </div> </div>If most people are playing major template characters, stacked minor templates might be an equaliser.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T06:44:07-08:00","id":1164775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164704-the-demon-blooded-dhampir?p=1164740#post1164740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering you can have vampire and changeling wolf-blooded I wouldn't consider a dhampir or ghoul or revenant as something you couldn't give a Tell to.<br /> <br /> Most people's aversion to template stacking seems to be an overly dramatic reaction to a NPC from World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> More realistically, a problem you'll have is that a demon-blooded or dhampir game is meant to be at a certain power level, and when one player has twice the 'power' of the others it's possible they're playing a character who is objectively more advantageous. It also can act to change the focus of the story a bit, as they are all generally tied to larger settings, dhampir to Vampire, fractals to Demon and so forth. If these are not problems, for whatever reason, then go wild. Have dhampir mages. If you're willing to put more work into the homebrew and ignore people on the forum telling you that it's impossible, have vampire mages, or demon vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sam Height wasn't a bad character because he crossed so many splats. He was a bad character because he was nonsensically powerful for no reason aside being &quot;that good at being bad&quot;.<br /> <br /> I do find the assumption of Major Templates not stacking fitting for two main reasons. First, because it isn't simple to do, and simply mashing things wouldn't do the trick very well. Second, because it is easier to make mixtures a special case for your chronicle than it is to ban them. The simplest assumption gives more space for tweaking the setting.<br /> <br /> But I think that a book about this kind of cross-over would be interesting. Something presenting new rules and templates, both Minor and Major, about what <u>can</u> happen when distinct magics meet each other in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'll later try again on the work I started after we had here a try at a Changeling-Vampire hybrid with some very interesting concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T13:54:35-08:00","id":1164883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164704-the-demon-blooded-dhampir?p=1164775#post1164775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do find the assumption of Major Templates not stacking fitting for two main reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Predators supplement for Werewolf gave a good way to describe it when saying why major supernaturals couldn't be Claimed. Humans are like raw clay, able to be moulded and shaped. While the amount of supernature that goes into a major splat is analagous to firing that clay - and once fired, clay isn't malleable any more - it can't be shaped and fired again, only shattered. Whether or not you want that to be true, it helps to have an in-universe way to express the inability (or difficulty).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I think that a book about this kind of cross-over would be interesting. Something presenting new rules and templates, both Minor and Major, about what <u>can</u> happen when distinct magics meet each other in the World of Darkness. </div> </div> </div>The Crossover Chronicle is coming, though I don't know if it will cover hybridising templates.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T15:29:44-08:00","id":1164906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164704-the-demon-blooded-dhampir?p=1164883#post1164883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Predators supplement for Werewolf gave a good way to describe it when saying why major supernaturals couldn't be Claimed. Humans are like raw clay, able to be moulded and shaped. While the amount of supernature that goes into a major splat is analagous to firing that clay - and once fired, clay isn't malleable any more - it can't be shaped and fired again, only shattered. Whether or not you want that to be true, it helps to have an in-universe way to express the inability (or difficulty).</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that limitation went away in second edition, and nothing seems to keep anyone from being claimed now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T15:33:49-08:00","id":1164908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164704-the-demon-blooded-dhampir#post1164704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm still not entirely sure what kind of stories might be interesting to explore with such characters, though. Perhaps a character that's the 'end result' of a long line of Ordo-Dracul research, some sort of Proto-Deviant?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd actually say it would be the other way around. Getting a wolf-blooded dhampir would be the end goal, a Deviant would be what happened when something fucked up. Or went horribly right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T15:41:04-08:00","id":1164913,"title":"","content":"Considering the ways to create wolf-blooded and dhampir are both really well known and fairly easy to replicate (providing you have access to a vampire and a werewolf or other wolf-blooded) it probably wouldn't take much work to do. Especially given how easy it is for both sides to guarantee conception (vampires through blood sorcery, werewolves through rites and spirit magic).<br /> <br /> You might want to throw some more variables into things if you want it to take a 'long line' of research or anywhere near what a Deviant is. Like creating a dhampir with natural Discipline powers or a Beast, or a wolf-blooded invisible to Luna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-03-2017, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T17:13:53-08:00","id":1164925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164704-the-demon-blooded-dhampir?p=1164906#post1164906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that limitation went away in second edition, and nothing seems to keep anyone from being claimed now.</div> </div> </div> </div>That may be so for Claimed, but it remains a good model to use if you want an in-world reason not to be able to hybridise major templates (for which the clay analogy is even more apt anyway).<br /> <br /> If.<br /> <br /> I have nothing against hybrids, except for the logisitcal problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T06:49:37-08:00","id":1165034,"title":"","content":"I have a weird PC who is trying to stay alive as long as possible in environment stacked with full-splat allies and antagonists. Thanks to reasons he was going to be a special family ghoul, but dhampir *looks* like a better fit except for Thief of Fate. So, I'll probably cobble together something appropriate that colors outside the lines as minimally as possible. <br /> <br /> Oh. And we've established that the PC is wolf-blooded, so definite minor-splatting is occurring. I expect this to be no problem, as wolf-blooded provides very minor mechanical benefits (Lunacy avoidance, mostly) and the effects of the Tell. <br /> <br /> I know very little about demon-blooded or whatever the equivalent for Changeling might be. That said the point is that combining minor splats is a viable strategy to bring a mortal PC up to functional agency when playing alongside full-splats. I see no reason to blanket restrict that in 2e.<br /> <br /> Samuel Height read like an intellectual exercise or some designer's campaign character foisted upon the fanbase at large--THAT is why he universally rubbed people the wrong way. We're building our own stories and our own special flowers need space to bloom.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}